      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Buren%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The Old Frisco Station, a Victorian railroad depot, once served the St. Louis–San Francisco Railway and now hosts film scenes.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        1,
        5
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Buren%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "The Crawford County Courthouse, built in 1842, is the oldest active courthouse west of the Mississippi River.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14,
        16
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia",
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Buren%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Van Buren’s name honors Martin Van Buren, the future U.S. president, after whom the town’s post office was named.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        21
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Van_Buren%2C_Arkansas"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The town’s historic trolley, an 1800s classic car, runs daily between Wednesday and Saturday, sharing stories at downtown stops.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18
